  "changes": {
    "reasoning_profiles": "welp-reasoning-topology 0.1.0-draft (new first-class methodology concept): every prospective campaign qualifies the model's ACTUAL reasoning topology experimentally on the pinned runtime (case A no reasoning mode; B reasoning present, no supported OFF; C effective supported ON/OFF control; D additional bounded effort levels) and records it in a hash-bound qualification record bound to the campaign manifest. Case C requires linked sibling Reasoning On AND Reasoning Off profile events — each a complete WELP campaign with its own profile identity, setup, calibration, ceilings, prompt/control binding, reliability, safety, real-work, context, performance, evidence bundle, classification and deployment guidance. Requested-but-ineffective OFF controls never create a Reasoning Off profile.",
    "evidence_binding": "Profile-invariant records (model source identity, license, artifact SHA-256, quant identity, architecture, runtime commit/build, physical hardware, load/fit qualification, unchanged template identity, artifact provenance) may be shared across sibling profile events only when explicitly marked in manifest.profile_invariant_evidence with hash-bound references. Behavioral evidence (calibration, ceilings, scored outputs, reliability, safety outcomes, capability modules, context cells, generation performance, latency, token consumption, classification) is profile-specific; cross-profile behavioral binding fails closed (validator R19). Evidence reused from a prior same-profile event carries explicit reuse provenance (class REUSE/REVALIDATE/RE-DERIVED/MUST_RERUN/INCOMPARABLE, source event/path/sha256).",
    "classification": "Per-profile independent classification is required; averaging, merging, scoring or verbally collapsing distinct profile verdicts into one model-level score is prohibited (validator R20). The publisher/default profile is recorded as context and never demotes the other supported profile(s). A case-C event whose sibling profile event is pending records an incomplete MODEL characterization (validator R21 warning; group completeness gates publication).",
    "effort_levels": "Bounded prospective effort-level policy (case D): additional ON effort levels are qualified (control effectiveness, reasoning/visible token use, completion behavior, latency, response characteristics, publisher guidance) and promoted to full profiles only when genuinely supported, measurably distinct, deployment-relevant and practically decisive; no unbounded sweep and no post-hoc best-mode search.",
    "performance_context_safety": "Performance (prefill, decode, answer latency, reasoning-token cost, visible-answer tokens, completion rate, TTFT/first-visible-answer where measurable, VRAM where materially different), Controlled Context and Multi-Document Context, safety tasks, and required real-work modules are characterized independently per full profile with the same frozen model-agnostic task set where applicable.",
    "architecture": "One WELP campaign event per full reasoning profile (linked sibling events sharing a reasoning group id), chosen over one-campaign-multi-bundle because per-event evidence/validation/publication machinery already exists, manifests never need post-hoc edits when a sibling completes, and the central registry already presents multiple profiles per model with explicit links. Historical single-profile campaigns remain valid unchanged under their frozen snapshots.",
    "validator": "validate_campaign_welp.py R18-R21 from snapshot date 2026-09-25: R18 topology+profile identity record and consistency (including no fake Reasoning Off and no unqualified promoted effort profiles); R19 profile evidence binding, invariant-only sharing and reuse provenance; R20 no model-level averaging in the publication export; R21 case-C group completeness. Frozen historical bundles are untouched and keep validating under their pinned snapshot hashes.",
    "schemas": "Additive optional properties: campaign manifest (reasoning_topology, reasoning_profile, profile_invariant_evidence), setup document (reasoning_profile), eval-profile descriptor (reasoning_profile, publisher_default_profile), website publication export (reasoning_profiles per-profile summaries).",
    "compatibility": "Older snapshots, retained campaign evidence, frozen manifests and historical reports stay immutable. Pre-2026-09-25 campaigns validate unchanged (era-gated rules; verified against the retained Ling and Granite hardening-era bundles at freeze)."
  },
